WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.716
Stress is a normal response to demand, uncertainty, and consequence.

00:00:03.716 --> 00:00:06.971
Some pressure can sharpen attention and create useful urgency.

00:00:06.971 --> 00:00:10.948
Too much pressure can narrow thinking, reduce patience, increase impulsive action,

00:00:10.948 --> 00:00:12.395
and make communication worse.

00:00:12.395 --> 00:00:17.457
Human performance improves when teams can tell the difference between useful activation and overload.

00:00:17.457 --> 00:00:19.989
Arousal and performance have a practical relationship.

00:00:19.989 --> 00:00:22.882
Very low activation can feel unfocused or disengaged.

00:00:22.882 --> 00:00:25.413
Moderate activation can support readiness and effort.

00:00:25.413 --> 00:00:28.306
Excessive activation can interfere with judgment and coordination.

00:00:28.306 --> 00:00:30.837
The point is not to eliminate stress.

00:00:30.837 --> 00:00:35.176
The point is to manage pressure so people can still think, communicate,

00:00:35.176 --> 00:00:36.261
and act deliberately.

00:00:36.261 --> 00:00:41.324
Emotional regulation is the ability to notice internal state and choose a useful response.

00:00:41.324 --> 00:00:44.578
Simple pause techniques, slow breathing, naming the next action,

00:00:44.578 --> 00:00:49.641
and asking for a short reset can help create space between stimulus and action.

00:00:49.641 --> 00:00:51.449
These are practical work techniques,

00:00:51.449 --> 00:00:55.788
not substitutes for qualified care when health or safety concerns are present.

00:00:55.788 --> 00:00:57.235
Preparation reduces avoidable stress.

00:00:57.235 --> 00:01:01.213
Pre-briefs clarify goals, roles, risks, and escalation paths before work begins.

00:01:01.213 --> 00:01:03.744
Debriefs help teams learn after the event.

00:01:03.744 --> 00:01:06.637
Good systems reduce uncertainty by making priorities, responsibilities,

00:01:06.637 --> 00:01:08.083
and decision rights visible.

00:01:08.083 --> 00:01:12.423
Under pressure, people should not have to invent the process from scratch.

00:01:12.423 --> 00:01:16.039
A practical habit is to name the next controllable step.

00:01:16.039 --> 00:01:20.740
Under pressure, people can become trapped in the size of the whole problem.

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:25.441
A clear next action narrows attention without denying the seriousness of the situation.

00:01:25.441 --> 00:01:29.780
This helps individuals and teams move from emotional reaction toward coordinated action.
